  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular Economy Summit on RMG in Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh&apos;s apparel and textile industry has achieved significant success as a global garments manufacturer but at a high environmental cost. The industry&apos;s exponential growth has resulted in waste generation, resource depletion, and pollution.Embracing circular economy principles offers a compelling solution to these challenges by transitioning from a linear model to one that promotes resource efficiency and waste reduction. Closing the loop through recycling, reusing, and designing for durability can yield numerous benefits.However, investment, technology and effective policy interventions are crucial to drive this transformation and support more circular business models. The first Bangladesh Circular Economy Summit (June 2023) will explore these three drivers for a transformation towards a more circular apparel and textile industry in Bangladesh.The Netherlands, via the Netherlands embassy in Dhaka, Bangladesh and Holland Circular Hotspot, will participate in this first Bangladesh Circular Economy Summit. It is expected that the summit will initiate to create a shared understanding of the circular economy and identify the opportunities for Bangladesh and to meet with CE stakeholders. The results will furthermore enable the Netherlands embassy in Dhaka, Bangladesh to develop a robust combi-track proposal for Circular Economy in the Garment Industry in Bangladesh.</narrative>
  </description>
